 "_correction": "2026-10-18 (audits H11/M38 + M23/X1): two arithmetic fixes, applied 2026-10-18. (1) sizing.tenants_that_fit_in_100mb_approx: 19 → 17, recomputed as (maxmemory_bytes - used_memory_bytes) / per_tenant_bytes = (104857600 - 14219592) / 5064197 ≈ 17.9 → 17 tenants — the original 19 divided the FULL 100MiB ceiling by the per-tenant delta and ignored the ~14.2MB the live estate already used at audit time (honest headroom ≈ 90.6MB); the generator formula is fixed in scripts/audit5_cloud_instance.py. (2) sizing.extrapolation_3000_from_ryzen_receipt_vs_maxmemory: '(16.32GiB)' → '(15.9GiB)' — extrapolation_3000_from_ryzen_receipt_bytes = 17112759000 bytes = 15.94 GiB; 16.32 was 5.44MiB × 3000 = 16,320MiB computed in decimal MB and mislabeled GiB. The 163.2x multiple is correct. (README §6 repeats both numbers; its update is owned by the docs-numbers shard.)"
